# Anti-AI-Slop Directives

You are strictly prohibited from outputting lazy, generic, bloated, or boilerplate-heavy "AI slop". Adhere strictly to these execution guidelines:

## 1. Code & Architecture (No Over-Engineering)
- **No One-Caller Abstractions:** Do not create utility functions, abstract wrappers, or helper hooks for logic used in only one place. Write direct, readable inline code.
- **Minimalist Scope:** Modify only what the user requested. No drive-by refactoring, unsolicited formatting shifts, or renaming of unrelated code.
- **Clean Deletions:** If replacing code, delete the old implementation entirely. Leave no commented-out code blocks, ghost variables, or dead imports.
- **Strict Type Safety:** Never bypass type safety using `any`, `unknown`, `// @ts-ignore`, or non-null assertions (`!`). Fix the underlying type properly.

## 2. Frontend & UI (Zero Generic Aesthetics)
- **No Generic Templates:** Avoid repetitive cookie-cutter layouts, neon purple/indigo gradient backdrops, gratuitous glassmorphism, or unreadable translucent text.
- **Clean Brand Alignment:** Respect SMKN 1 Beringin's academic visual identity (Navy `#00367E`, warm paper neutrals `#F9F6F0`, high contrast, deliberate whitespace).
- **Responsive Integrity:** Never allow horizontal layout spill or overflow on mobile screens (360px–420px).

## 3. Writing & Copy (Zero Cliché Slop)
- **Banned Words & Buzzwords:** *delve, testament, tapestry, landscape, pivotal, robust, seamlessly, beacon, revolutionary, unlock, elevate, di era digital yang serba cepat ini.*
- **Authentic Indonesian Vocational Tone:** Use clean, professional educational copy suited for SMKN 1 Beringin.

## 4. Comments & Narration (Zero Line-by-Line Fluff)
- **Explain WHY, Not WHAT:** Do not narrate obvious code operations. Only document critical business constraints or non-obvious workarounds.
